{"id": "section-body-09455", "title": "Anal Fissures", "chapterId": "chapter-ten", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "GASTROINTESTINAL DISEASE CONDITIONS", "Diseases of the Intestine", "Anal Fissures"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-09455", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Anal Fissures", "runs": [{"text": "Anal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Fissures"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1531"}}, {"id": "body-09456", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "These are painful linear ulcers in the anal canal. Young and middle-aged adults most affected. Primary fissure occurs in the posterior midline. It can also be secondary to Crohn’s disease, anal cancer, or infection such as syphilis, TB in which case they occur more lateral. Passage of hard stools is a common predisposition to primary fissures.", "runs": [{"text": "These are painful linear ulcers in the anal canal. Young and middle-aged adults most affected. Primary fissure occurs in the posterior"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "midline."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "also"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "secondary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Crohn’s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disease,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "anal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cancer,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "such"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "syphilis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "TB"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "they occur more lateral. Passage of hard stools is a common predisposition to primary fissures."}]}, {"id": "body-09458", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presen